  ],
  "notes": "Drawn from the left side (2026-05-30, side-on; the quote's heights from the near-level 2026-05 photo at Seattle, as the approach photo from below lifted them about a tenth of the body's half-height, onto the windows) and Alaska's photo of the right side. The two sides carry different quotes (titles marked by side); the right side's quote is placed from Alaska's three-quarter photo, so its position is less sure. The profiles are drawn as one copper field with an amber front: each face is in the logo entry. The 'UNCF' logo on the engines and the small quote attributions aren't drawn. Re-drawn 2026-11-28: the right side from Alaska's press photo (sunlit, right side from ahead), registered by the forward door, the overwing exits and the aft door, heights under the door sills scaled to the belly. Mandela's quote had been one guessed block across the windows: it's three italic lines over the windows ('EDUCATION' off-white, 'IS THE MOST POWERFUL' and 'WEAPON WE' orange, 'CAN' off-white) and two under them ('USE TO' orange, 'CHANGE' off-white, then a small 'THE' and the big 'WORLD.'). Two-color lines are two titles each. The small 'IS' on the left and both attributions are now drawn. The profiles' areas are the photo's big color fields (amber, copper, dark brown, the black between the heads) from over the wing to the aft door, mirrored on the left as the left-side photos show; under the wing, which hides them, the necks and shoulders are carried straight down. Color changes: 'amber' #E8892F to #F4A12E (the sunlit press photo); 'plum' #4A3236 added for the dark brown heads at the crown. Cleaned up 2026-11-28 after review: the fin's 'Alaska' measured against the fin on the left-side photo (2026-05-30) and Alaska's press photo: about 0.25 of the fin's span tall, running from near the root at mid-chord toward the tip at about 61 degrees, ending clear of the tip and the leading edge as both sides' photos show (it had been half that size). Color change: 'bone' #DAD6CE to #F1EDE2, the quotes' off-white as the sunlit press photo shows it (it read grey by the nose).",
  "from": "2021-04",
